{\b\fs22 Interview Recorder - before you install}\par\par
{\b What this program does}\par
Interview Recorder records consented research interviews held in Google Meet: the meeting audio played on this PC and your microphone, as two separate tracks. After you stop, it transcribes the audio offline and saves an audio-only MP4 file and an editable Word document in your Documents\\Interview Recorder folder.\par\par
{\b Privacy}\par
The program works fully offline. It makes no network connections, sends no audio or transcripts anywhere, has no telemetry and needs no account. Recording never starts without your action, and a recording indicator is always visible.\par\par
{\b Your responsibilities}\par
Get informed consent and the research approvals your institution requires before you record. Use a pseudonymous participant ID, not a name. Keep the data folder out of cloud sync folders (OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive, iCloud). Turn on BitLocker or Windows device encryption: the program's files are not encrypted by the program itself. Software alone cannot make a study POPIA compliant.\par\par
{\b Limitations}\par
Automatic transcripts can contain errors and can miss very short turns. Check every transcript against the audio. Ordinary system-audio capture can include other sounds playing on this PC: use headphones and close other programs that play sound.\par\par
{\b Third-party software}\par
This program includes NAudio, Whisper.net and whisper.cpp with the Whisper base model, the Open XML SDK, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm and the .NET runtime (all MIT licence), and an LGPL build of FFmpeg run as a separate program. Details and licence texts: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md in the installation folder.\par\par
The program is provided as is, without warranty of any kind.\par
